SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The ccoommpprreessss, uunnccoommpprreessss, and zzccaatt utilities are compliant with the
     X/Open System Interfaces option of the IEEE Std 1003.1-2008 (“POSIX.1”)
     specification.

     The ccoommpprreessss flags [--112233445566778899ddgghhllNNnnOOooqqrrSStt], uunnccoommpprreessss flags
     [--hhllNNnnooqqrrtt], and the zzccaatt flags [--ffgghhqqrr] are extensions to that specifi‐
     cation.

     IEEE Std 1003.1-2008 (“POSIX.1”) specifies a maximum bits limit (--bb) of
     14 to "achieve portability to all systems".

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ccoommpprreessss command appeared in 4.3BSD.  Deflate compression support was
     added in OpenBSD 2.1.

